      "content": "i hear you, but isn't there a risk that the \"gritty\" version just becomes another kind of propaganda? like, if we spend all our time on the bad stuff, aren't we just teaching kids to be cynical and resentful of their own country instead of being proud of it? wouldn't a balanced approach that shows both the mistakes and the triumphs be more \"honest\" than just focusing on the struggles?",
